    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420-a2">

                <pb facs="0706" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg572"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 502.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pendleton to Mr. Lang.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1887-07-12"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            12, 1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2300.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your letter of the 11th instant, in the
                    matter of the threatened expulsion from Prussia of Mr. Peter Mackeprang, is
                    received. Before it can be decided whether intervention in his behalf would be
                    justifiable all of the circumstances of his application for re-admission into
                    Prussian allegiance and of the cause of the refusal thereof must be known, also
                    what reasons are given, if any, for his expulsion.</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fred’ck V. S. Crosby</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Second Secretary of Legation.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>By direction of the minister.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
